# The builder stage does `COPY . .`, so anything ignored by git but present on
# disk still enters the build context and is baked into a layer. These are all
# gitignored (see .gitignore) yet were shipping real credentials:
#   .seed-creds       plaintext passwords for the five role accounts
#   rotate-creds.mjs  had a production admin password as a literal fallback
#   check-*.js        ad-hoc API probing against production
.seed-creds
rotate-*.mjs
check-*.js
fix-*.js
verify-*.js
list-users.js
test-*.sh
=193
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage